/-!
# Central geometry and the contrary Sylow choice in 15.4.19–20

Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed pp.1163–1164.
The raw factor decompositions and conjugation witnesses construct the fixed
lines, hyperplanes, and all conclusions of 15.4.19 for every factor choice.
The quotient and Sylow inputs of 15.4.12 give index three in each generated
factor group and force the four intersections to equal `T₀`.

Failure of the final Sylow assertion yields a larger Sylow subgroup of maximal
order. Baumann normalizer control and the actual factor permutations conjugate
it into `T`, preserve `T₀`, and transport the generated group to another of the
four choices. The larger subgroup remains Sylow in every subsequent
`H`-overgroup, including the normalizer of the intrinsic two-core. Both indices
are two, and a moved factor generates its whole product.

The index-two placement proves characteristic-normalizer control of
`R=O₂(XT_I)`. Its radicality, intrinsic characteristic-normalizer control,
SQTK inheritance and Sylow property in the subgroup generated by its
`I₀∩M₁`-conjugates construct all clauses of Hypothesis C.2.3. The corrected
normalizer Sylow statement also constructs the 1.1.5 hypotheses. Actual
factor images in the full `S₃ × S₃` quotient construct independent inversion
and interchange, canonical intrinsic Xi membership, the full local 1.3.2
inputs, and an inverting Frattini commutator. The old signed-coordinate
interfaces are preserved. The two-residual Borel fixes both factors and their commutator
modules; faithful inner action on an actual binary linear component is
excluded using its computed Sylow center.

The placed counterexample now retains the global maximal Sylow-order
bound after conjugation. Both two-perfect factors lie in the actual
prime-to-three residual, and replacement by that residual times `T_I`
retains all corrected Sylow assertions. Odd-prime PSL₂ components at primes
at least seven are excluded from faithful inner action, using relative
subnormality and the actual ambient Sylow subgroup. For PSL₂(5) pairs,
the genuine component projections and their intertwined actions bound the
quotient action image by two, incompatible with the constructed D₈ image.

The canonical Sylow-complement equivalence identifies its normalizer automizer
with this quotient action image. The exact intrinsic embedding input retains
the additional Sylow hypothesis required by the corrected local 1.3.4.

The source configuration must still realize the displayed decomposition,
permutation and full product-quotient witnesses. The quotient action is now
identified with the actual D₈ group, allowing signed exchangers of order four.
Full embedding alternatives, identification of the component product with
the residual, Borel/root/module placements and both source case
eliminations remain open. These exports do not assert full 15.4.20 or construct
`Source.LocalData`.
-/
